# SABOTAGE: PP-13 (tenant reveal-approver surface) — drops the tenant `org_id` from the
# approve-moment `granted` audit in `Samen.Reveal.Grants.do_approve/4`, sending it to the
# reserved `__global__` operator chain instead of the tenant's own audit chain. This is the
# exact Batch-6 residual PP-13 closed: with `org_id: nil` the "granted" event no longer shows
# on the tenant's `Settings.SecurityLive` "Reveal access" ledger (`reveal_events_for_org/2`
# filters `grant_lifecycle` on the org chain), so the moment PII was authorized to unmask is
# invisible to the tenant again. The `approve-audit-on-tenant-chain-must-flip-a-named-test` pin.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/reveal_approver_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: on the tenant audit chain, org-attributed
# APPLY: git apply scripts/sabotages/189-pp13-reveal-approver-approve-audit-off-tenant-chain.patch
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/reveal/grants.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/reveal/grants.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/reveal/grants.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/reveal/grants.ex
@@ -334,7 +334,7 @@
           actor_id: granted_by,
           request_id: req.id,
           grant_id: grant_id,
-          org_id: Map.get(opts, :org_id),
+          org_id: nil,
           detail: "expires_at=#{DateTime.to_iso8601(expires_at)}"
         })
       end)
